// Pokémon data, organized by region. Each entry's "id" is its National
// Pokédex number. The Home screen (National Dex) lists every entry here
// sorted by id; tapping a region chip filters down to just that region.
// REGIONS (in ../data.js) lists every mainline region so the region bar
// always shows a button for each one, even before that region's Pokémon
// have been added.
//
// Today's core flat fields are id, name, region, plus these OPTIONAL ones —
// already understood by the detail screen with no code change: types,
// category, height, weight, abilities, description. "abilities" should be
// a list of ability NAMES (looked up in data/abilities.js), not inline
// descriptions — the full description for each ability lives there once,
// not repeated per Pokémon.
//
// Species flags from pokemon_species.csv (0.2.1, TODO.md #10) — data only,
// nothing on the detail screen renders them yet: isLegendary / isMythical /
// isBaby are written only when true (absent means false), and genderRate is
// -1 for a genderless species, otherwise 0-8 eighths-female (0 = male-only,
// 8 = female-only).
//
// Second data-only batch (0.2.5, same TODO.md #10 list), appended after
// `description` on every entry that has them — still nothing UI-wired:
//   hasGenderDifferences  pokemon_species.csv has_gender_differences, written
//                         only when true. Distinct from `hasFemaleSprite`
//                         (which means "we bundled the art"), though today
//                         the two happen to cover the same 95 entries.
//   habitat               resolved display name from pokemon_habitats.csv
//                         ("Cave", "Rough Terrain", ...). Absent for most
//                         Gen 4+ species — the column is FireRed/LeafGreen-era
//                         and simply blank for them, not missing data.
//   formsSwitchable       forms_switchable, written only when true.
//   baseExperience        pokemon.csv base_experience for the default forme —
//                         exp yield on defeat.
//   regionalDexNumbers    that species' number in each mainline region's own
//                         dex ({ kanto: 1, johto: 226 }), in REGIONS order.
//                         Absent when a species has none. KALOS IS NEVER A
//                         KEY: it has three sub-dexes and no single
//                         national-style regional dex to pick from, so it is
//                         skipped rather than merged by a guessed rule (see
//                         tools/populate_region.js regionalPokedexes()).
//                         Hisui is also absent — data/hisui.js already owns
//                         that dex's numbering.
//   eggGroups             (0.2.7, UI-wired: the Facts card's "Egg Groups"
//                         row) English names from egg_group_prose.csv, 1-2
//                         per species ("Monster", "Water 1", "Undiscovered").

